WEBVTT

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:05.490
A professional executive partnership makes work clear and commitments reliable

00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:10.055
In this unit you will translate priorities into support deliverables

00:00:10.055 --> 00:00:15.490
prepare a usable working agreement distinguish role boundaries present options

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:19.410
when demands conflict and arrange a concern route and sustainable

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:23.605
cover Your two main work products are a working agreement

00:00:23.605 --> 00:00:28.190
and a priority decision brief The Meridian people and arrangements

00:00:28.190 --> 00:00:35.235
are fictional Numerical examples are case facts not operating standards

00:00:35.235 --> 00:00:39.615
The course does not grant workplace authority You will follow

00:00:39.615 --> 00:00:43.930
Daniel as he supports Lindiwe at Meridian Start with the

00:00:43.930 --> 00:00:48.515
facts available at 07:40 make your own first brief and

00:00:48.515 --> 00:00:52.850
only then compare the later confirmed record Use the glossary

00:00:52.850 --> 00:00:57.255
for unfamiliar words and the source reading for detail Practice

00:00:57.255 --> 00:01:01.455
activities help you learn without adding to your formal mark

00:01:01.455 --> 00:01:04.655
The separate formative test lets you try the agreed question

00:01:04.655 --> 00:01:09.335
and quiz retry rules Keep your practical portfolio as a

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:13.715
draft for later feedback You can pause or replay narration

00:01:13.715 --> 00:01:18.025
and read the same material as text Use only fictional

00:01:18.025 --> 00:01:21.690
or sanitised information in your responses
